    {
      "id": "CV5-inner-refusal-message-echoes-the-declared-version",
      "file": "src/copper_mcp/board_ir/codec.py",
      "anchor": "                SCHEMA_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED,\n                _SCHEMA_VERSION_REFUSAL,\n                \"snapshot.schema_version\",\n            )\n        content = _decode_content",
      "replacement": "                SCHEMA_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED,\n                f\"{_SCHEMA_VERSION_REFUSAL} (declared {envelope['schema_version']!r})\",\n                \"snapshot.schema_version\",\n            )\n        content = _decode_content",
      "expectation": "equivalent",
      "killing_tests": [
        "tests/test_board_ir_schema.py::test_the_version_refusal_never_echoes_the_version_the_document_declared"
      ],
      "equivalence_argument": "Unobservable through the public surface by construction. Every BoardIRValidationError raised inside decode_snapshot_json's try block is caught by `except BoardIRValidationError as error: validation_code = error.code`, which keeps the code and discards the message; the caller receives whichever message the tail re-raise chooses. So the message at this site cannot reach a caller no matter what it is built from. This was found by running the mutant, not by inspection -- it was declared killed first and reported as survived. It is left in the spec because the survival is the evidence: it proves the non-echo property is enforced by the normalisation and not by the test. CV6 mutates the tail, which is the site that can echo, and is killed there."
    },
